  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "$$\n{\u222d}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{\u2217}^{\u2217}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{\u2217}^{\u2217}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz\n$$\n\nGiven that the triple integral above is considered over the rectangular box\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le e,\\,1\\le z\\le \\operatorname{ln}\u20613},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$",
  "worked_solution": "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\u222d}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u20613}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{e}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a+b=-2+3=1.$",
